call mtr.add_suppression("Component audit_log_filter reported: 'Wrong JSON filter '.*' format");
call mtr.add_suppression("Component audit_log_filter reported: 'Skipping disabled event");
call mtr.add_suppression("Component audit_log_filter reported: 'audit_log_filter name: .*, filter: .* has wrong format");
# Change user picks up the new account filter
# Named character and numeric-looking FULL-mode field
# REDUCED load skips a disabled class and keeps the table predicate
# Restart keeps the stored filter
# Unload stops filtering and reinstall restores it
# Named character still matches after the component is reinstalled
# Two clients, ten inserts each
# Open sessions keep the previous filter across a reload
# Removing one account applies on that account's next connection
regex reload OK
